            "unit": "configurations"
          }
        },
        "results_json": {
          "power_conversion_efficiency_without_barrier": {
            "value": 0.37,
            "unit": "%"
          },
          "power_conversion_efficiency_with_barrier": {
            "value": 1.5,
            "unit": "%"
          }
        },
        "source_text": "Javaid et al. have alleviated this issue by utilizing a thin barrier layer at the junction (in this case, Al2O3 ) to act as a barrier to recombination, increasing the efficiency of ZnSnN2 photovoltaics from 0.37% to 1.5%, despite the non-ideal band offsets of the ZnSnN2 /SnO junction used (Fig. 6 (d))."
      },
